Modifications
-------------
  Modified by SkyTekx (the ts4.party community), 2026, for the SkyTekx 3 modpack. This build runs
  on Minecraft 1.20.1 with Forge 47, Cucumber 7.0.16 and Mystical Agriculture 7.0.24, keeps the mod
  id mysticalautomation, its registry ids and NBT keys, and is versioned 1.0.8-skytekx.1.

  Summary of the changes:
    * Port: the Java sources target Forge 47 (DeferredRegister, block entity capabilities, a
      SimpleChannel with protocol version 1, menu screens in client setup, a COMMON config) and
      the APIs of Cucumber 7 and Mystical Agriculture 7 (its Machine Upgrades, altar and enchanter
      recipes). Container data travels as 16 bit halves and slot counts above 127 travel in an
      extra message, since 1.20.1 sends them as shorts and bytes. The fuel and progress widgets draw
      their lit part from the vanilla furnace texture at runtime.
    * Data: recipes, loot tables and tags in the 1.20.1 folders and fields, forge: tags in place of
      the c: tags, a pack.mcmeta.
    * Fixes: ghost slot and machine mode messages from clients only act on the open menu and its
      ghost slots, the Enchanternator takes the ingredients of the level it enchants at and the item
      it enchants, the JEI recipe transfer no longer reads past its slot views, and bone meal costs
      the full fuel usage of the Fertilizer. The Crafter refuses special recipes and recipes
      without a required input (the second check after upstream 7a481dc of the 26.1 line), which
      upstream crafted from ghost items alone. The Crafter and both Altarnators take real inputs
      that equal their ghost items, NBT included, and assemble the result from the items they take,
      not from the ghost grid. The Farmer adds each result to its outputs once and waits while
      they are full instead of dropping results.
    * Left out: the CraftTweaker integration and its test scripts.
    * Build: ForgeGradle for Forge 1.20.1 on Java 17, reproducible jar (no file timestamps, fixed
      entry order, no build timestamp in the manifest). mods.toml marks the build as a modified,
      unofficial one, sends bug reports to SkyTekx and drops the upstream update URL.

  The complete source of this build, with every change as a separate commit, is in
  https://github.com/skytekx/skytekx3-1201-server under ports/mysticalautomation.
  ports/mysticalautomation/UPSTREAM.md lists every change to the upstream build.

